{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"safe and unsafe agent actions safe and unsafe agent actions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","fileName":"Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"safe and unsafe agent actions safe and unsafe agent actions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","fileName":"Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions","heading":"Safe and Unsafe Agent Actions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Safe agent actions in CI/CD are usually observational or advisory: classify a failure, summarize tests, draft documentation, suggest a pull request, or identify a likely remediation. These activities improve understanding without directly changing production state.\n\nUnsafe actions include auto-merging protected branches, deploying to production, disabling failing tests, and modifying security policy. An agent trying to complete a goal may remove the very control that exposed a problem. Capability design should therefore distinguish useful analysis from authority that can bypass evidence, review, or recovery.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaif